From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Smith <thomsmit@google.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:32:58 -0700
Subject: [M150-LTS] cc, gpu: Widen PaintCacheId and paint cache deletion IPC
 to uint64_t

Skia is widening SkPath generation IDs from 32-bit to 64-bit. This CL
prepares Chromium to consume 64-bit IDs by widening PaintCacheId and
its associated serialization and GPU command buffer purging pipeline.

Bug: 562038679
Bug: 556268833
Change-Id: I6546900f138050327229c14db45c3c70b1e9640e
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8429709
Reviewed-by: Kyle Charbonneau <kylechar@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Robert Phillips <robertphillips@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Thomas Smith <thomsmit@google.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703606}
(cherry picked from commit 7ff661871690f30cb1912652aaaab2eadc23903f)

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y):
  - M148 does not wrap memcmp() in UNSAFE_TODO() in the generated
    *_cmd_format_test_autogen.h files or in build_cmd_buffer_lib.py, so the
    conflicting hunks were resolved keeping the plain memcmp() form. All 42
    autogen files were regenerated with build_raster_cmd_buffer.py and
    build_gles2_cmd_buffer.py and match the committed tree byte-for-byte.
  - M148 lacks the PaintOpWriter::Write(uint64_t) overload that main gained in
    crrev.com/c/8408827 ("Widen cc::PaintShader record shader IDs to 64
    bits"), so Write(id) with the widened PaintCacheId was ambiguous. That
    overload (declaration + two-uint32 implementation) is included here
    verbatim from 8408827; the rest of 8408827 is not picked.

